Fix the ParaLLEl-RSP JIT on hosts with 16 KB pages (Raspberry Pi 4/5).

The JIT allocator of the RSP reserves one large mapping and commits windows
of it with mprotect(). Upstream aligns those windows to 4 KB everywhere
except Apple silicon, but mprotect() rejects an address that is not aligned
to the real page size. On a 16 KB page kernel the second allocation fails,
the RSP calls abort() and takes the whole Kodi process down a few hundred
milliseconds into the first N64 game (SIGABRT in
RSP::JIT::CPU::jit_region). Use the real page size on every POSIX host.

Apply with: git -C <src> apply <this file>

--- a/mupen64plus-rsp-paraLLEl/jit_allocator.cpp
+++ b/mupen64plus-rsp-paraLLEl/jit_allocator.cpp
@@ -36,11 +36,11 @@ Allocator::~Allocator()
 
 static size_t align_page(size_t offset)
 {
-#if defined(__APPLE__) && defined(__aarch64__)
+	// mprotect() rejects a region whose address is not aligned to the real
+	// host page size. The hardcoded 4 KB mask breaks every kernel with 16 KB
+	// pages (Raspberry Pi 4/5): the second JIT allocation fails and the RSP
+	// aborts, taking Kodi down with it.
 	size_t pagesize = sysconf(_SC_PAGESIZE) - 1;
-#else
-	size_t pagesize = 4095;
-#endif
 	return (offset + pagesize) & ~size_t(pagesize);
 }
 
